description:
The production-host work carried out of the dev-box staging beads (6B.11 to 6B.13, PRs #72 to #79) when GATE-STAGING was signed off on 2026-10-22. Needs the owner's explicit go: it touches the production VPS. Sequenced by the pilot and cutover plan.

Secrets and access:
- deploy unit ExecStartPre refuses a secrets directory that is not 0700 or has writable secret files;
- preflight refuses CATALYST_STAFF_PUBLISH of 0.0.0.0 or ::;
- pg_hba: administrator only from provisioning; the backup login local-socket only (026 section 6);
- persistent host-owned Caddy /data.

Deploy:
- the force-command makes CATALYST_EXPECTED_COMMIT mandatory and keeps the host checkout at the deployed commit;
- parameterise the egress service's CATALYST_ENV (render_staging_compose hardcodes staging);
- confirm the deploy wrapper runs serially (the record has no lock);
- release checklist: RunSQL/RunPython migrations are reviewer-owned for expand-safety.

Backup and restore:
- forward-only.json in the host backup set;
- scheduled backups with receipts, archived into the host backup fabric;
- custody storage pointing inside the custody volume the restore writes into;
- receipt.sh failures wired into the alert floor;
- decide whether --expect-manifest-sha256 is mandatory in the production restore (default: mandatory).

Monitoring:
- install the health and liveness-sweep timers with OnFailure surfacing exit 3, plus the backup-freshness and restore-drill-overdue signals;
- with POL-16, decide whether provisioning_revocation_needs_staff moves to the age-graced routine set (each withdrawal pages today).

Cutover rehearsals before the live switch (from PR #79):
- the Learn error log's token filter with a dead upstream carrying a sentinel;
- an adverse import-order stand-in;
- the unix socket's ownership for the Learn Caddy user.
